      {
        "case_id": "F04",
        "answer": "During a billing\u2011profile migration, auto\u2011pay is automatically paused. It will not restart until the account owner confirms the new default payment method\u202f\u2014\u202fthis prevents any charge attempts against a payment method that may have failed re\u2011verification\u202f[HC\u2011BILL\u2011003--auto\u2011pay\u2011behavior\u2011after\u2011migration--prose\u2011001].  \n\nIf a billing cycle occurs while migration is in progress, the invoice is still generated but payment is deferred. Once migration completes and auto\u2011pay is re\u2011enabled (after the owner confirms the payment method), any deferred invoices are paid immediately in chronological order. A 7\u2011day grace period applies, and late\u2011payment fees are not assessed for invoices that become due during the migration window, provided they are paid within that period\u202f[HC\u2011BILL\u2011001--recurring\u2011billing\u2011and\u2011auto\u2011pay\u2011impact--prose\u2011001].",
